# Root build context exclusions. The service Dockerfiles (backend/Dockerfile,
# frontend/Dockerfile) normally build from their own directory and carry their
# own .dockerignore; this file protects any build that uses the repository root
# as context (a compose override, a one-off `docker build .`) from shipping
# secrets, the git history, node_modules or design assets into an image.
.git
.github
.gitleaks.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Documentation, design and agent material never belong in an image
docs
design
agents
*.md
!frontend/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

# Language and tool caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/coverage.xml

# Test and scan artefacts
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
sarif-results
.cache

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
